{
  "name": "62 - INTERNAL - Gmail Status",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Answers \"is Gmail connected yet?\"\n\nThe chat polls this while the learner is away in Google's sign-in window, so\nit knows the moment to carry on by itself. It reads the mailbox address and\nnothing else: no message bodies, no model call, no writes.\n\nIt deliberately writes no tool_audit row. The chat asks every couple of\nseconds while a connection is in progress, and auditing that would bury the\nreal tool calls under hundreds of polls.\n\nThe agent's own check is `69 - TOOL - check_gmail_connection`, which is where\nthe explaining lives. This one only ever answers yes or no.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-900, -280],
      "id": "95620000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Read this first"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "GET",
        "path": "gmail-status",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [-660, -60],
      "id": "95620000-0000-4000-8000-000000000010",
      "name": "Status Asked For",
      "webhookId": "95620000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000ff"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/me/profile",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "googleOAuth2Api",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "fullResponse": true,
              "neverError": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "position": [-420, -60],
      "id": "95620000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011",
      "name": "Probe Gmail",
      "credentials": {
        "googleOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "phase16GmailReadonly",
          "name": "Gmail (read-only)"
        }
      },
      "alwaysOutputData": true,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "const raw = $input.first().json ?? {};\nconst status = Number(raw.statusCode ?? 0);\nconst body = raw.body ?? {};\n\n// Connected means one thing only: Google answered with a mailbox. Every other\n// outcome is 'not yet', because the chat is only waiting to learn when it can\n// carry on. Why it is not connected is the agent's job to explain, in 69,\n// where there is room to say something the learner can act on.\nconst connected = status === 200 && Boolean(body.emailAddress);\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  schemaVersion: 1,\n  connected,\n  emailAddress: connected ? String(body.emailAddress) : '',\n} }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [-180, -60],
      "id": "95620000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012",
      "name": "Shape Status"
    },
